<title>FRANCE: Credit National sees 8.4 pct ROE in 1998.</title>
<headline>Credit National sees 8.4 pct ROE in 1998.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-09-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>French bank Credit National said on Tuesday cost cuts and the streamlining of operations after buying the BFCE bank should allow it to achieve a return on equity of around 8.4 percent by 1998.</p>
<p>The forecast came in a results statement in which the group announced that it had turned in a first-half net attributable loss of 112 million francs, after provisions for restructuring, versus a pro-forma 1995 first-half profit of 267 million francs. bfl</p>
</text>
